# Shell Gas Station - Business Logic Notes

## Business Case
Track how many fuel customers also visit the in-store convenience shop
to understand cross-sell conversion and improve revenue per visit.

## Data Model

### customers
- Unique customer per loyalty account or visit profile
- 60% are loyalty members with tiered status: Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum
- Fields: customer_id, full_name, email, phone, zip_code, loyalty_member,
          loyalty_tier, member_since, preferred_fuel

### fuel_transactions
- One row per fuel fill-up event
- Linked to customer via customer_id
- Fields: fuel_txn_id, customer_id, transaction_ts, pump_number, fuel_type,
          gallons, price_per_gallon, total_fuel_cost, payment_method,
          loyalty_points_earned (10 pts/gallon for members)

### store_purchases
- One row per line item in a store basket
- Linked back to the originating fuel_txn_id for conversion analysis
- Store visit timestamped 2-15 minutes after fuel fill-up
- Fields: store_item_id, fuel_txn_id, customer_id, purchase_id, store_ts,
          category, product_name, unit_price, quantity, line_total, basket_total

## Key Business Rules
- Conversion rate: 38% of pumpers also enter the store (STORE_CONVERSION = 0.38)
- Items per basket: 1-4 items per store visit
- Loyalty points: earned on fuel only, 10 pts per gallon, loyalty members only
- Store categories (probability-weighted):
    Beverages  35%  $1.99 - $5.49
    Snacks     25%  $0.99 - $4.99
    Hot Food   15%  $2.99 - $8.99
    Tobacco    10%  $7.99 - $14.99
    Car Care    8%  $3.99 - $24.99
    Lottery     4%  $1.00 - $20.00
    Automotive  3%  $4.99 - $39.99

## Key Metrics to Analyze
- Overall pump-to-store conversion rate
- Conversion by loyalty tier (do Gold/Platinum members shop more?)
- Conversion by fuel type or payment method
- Average basket size for store visitors
- Top-selling categories among pumpers
- Time gap between fueling and store entry

## Data Volumes (synthetic)
- 500 customers
- 5,000 fuel transactions (~10 visits per customer over 2025)
- ~1,900 store line items (~1,300 unique store visits at 38% conversion)

